; Entity handler: hanged man going up on his rope (room 9)
;
; The second half of the patrol of a hanged man of room 9 (Hangman tree). The first half, going down, is #R$B2F9 (kind
; 6 of the room object table); no room record has kind 7, a slot only gets this handler through the turn-round in
; #R$B2F9. Entity handlers are entered with SP at slot+2 (the RET of #R$A5E9 popped the handler word); they pop the
; words they need, push back the ones they change and end by jumping to #R$A5F0 with HL at the next slot.
; .
; The y coordinate goes up by the speed each frame. When its high byte falls below the upper turning point the handler
; word of the slot is rewritten with #R$B2F9, so the body goes down again from the next frame. The sprite is placed
; at (x, y), then the rope is redrawn in the tile map: the cell in the second column of the sprite, on the row of its
; top edge, gets TILE_ROPE (a dotted red line) and the cell below it TILE_BLANK, so the rope shortens as the body
; rises. Observed in room 9: the writes at $B279/$B27F change the map when the body rises and #R$B2F9's at
; $B33A/$B340 when it falls. The tail #R$B2CE tests the hit box against Jean and draws the sprite.
; .
; Slot fields used: +2 word speed (8.8, 2-pixel units per frame), +4 byte upper turning point of y, +5 byte lower
; turning point, +6 word x (only the high byte matters; it is a multiple of 4, so the sprite never needs a shift
; phase), +8 word y (8.8). The other fields are described at #R$B2D4.
; .
; Hardware: none. Writes the tile map at $5B00, which the draw queue shows.
;
; SP Slot address + 2
@label=UpdateHangedUp
c$B236 POP BC        ; speed
 $B237 POP DE        ; D lower turning point, E upper
 $B238 POP HL        ; x (8.8); only its high byte is used
 $B239 LD A,H        ; A = x in 2-pixel units
 $B23A EX AF,AF'     ; kept in A'
 $B23B POP HL        ; y (8.8)
 $B23C OR A          ;
 $B23D SBC HL,BC     ; y goes up
 $B23F PUSH HL       ; store y
 $B240 POP HL        ; SP is back at slot+$A
 $B241 LD A,H        ; y in 2-pixel units
 $B242 CP E          ; above the upper turning point?
 $B243 JR NC,$B253   ; no: go on
 $B245 LD HL,$FFF8   ; -8: back to slot+2
 $B248 ADD HL,SP     ;
 $B249 LD SP,HL      ;
 $B24A LD HL,$B2F9   ; from the next frame the body goes down
 $B24D PUSH HL       ; written over the handler word at slot+0
 $B24E POP HL        ; pop the handler again
 $B24F POP BC        ; pop speed, limits, x and y again
 $B250 POP DE        ;
 $B251 POP HL        ;
 $B252 POP HL        ;
*$B253 EX AF,AF'     ; A = x
 $B254 LD D,A        ; D = x
 $B255 POP BC        ; skip the unused word at +$A
 $B256 LD E,H        ; E = y
 $B257 LD L,H        ; L = y
 $B258 LD H,D        ; H = x
 $B259 LD A,H        ;
 $B25A EX AF,AF'     ; A' = x: its low two bits are the shift phase
 $B25B SRA H         ; x / 4: byte column
 $B25D SRA H         ;
 $B25F LD ($ACD3),HL ; draw command position: (y, x/4)
 $B262 SRA L         ; y / 4: row of cells
 $B264 SRA L         ;
 $B266 LD A,L        ; low byte of the map offset: (row mod 8) * 32 + column
 $B267 RRCA          ;
 $B268 RRCA          ;
 $B269 RRCA          ;
 $B26A LD L,A        ;
 $B26B AND $E0       ;
 $B26D ADD A,H       ;
 $B26E LD H,A        ;
 $B26F LD A,L        ;
 $B270 AND $03       ; high byte: row / 8
 $B272 LD L,H        ;
 $B273 LD H,A        ;
 $B274 INC L         ; second column of the sprite
@isub=LD BC,TILE_MAP
 $B275 LD BC,$5B00   ;
 $B278 ADD HL,BC     ;
@isub=LD (HL),TILE_ROPE
 $B279 LD (HL),$B7   ; rope on the row of the top edge
@isub=LD BC,SCREEN_COLS
 $B27B LD BC,$0020   ;
 $B27E ADD HL,BC     ; the cell below
@isub=LD (HL),TILE_BLANK
 $B27F LD (HL),$80   ; no rope below the end
 $B281 JR $B2CE      ; hit box test and draw
